format: 2
name: a diamond Tuple3 with a declared target type encodes its components (#299)
class: Probe
method: m
arg: 03
arg: 04
expect: AGREE
note: ADR-068 D4 exception 2 (#299): with a typed target the diamond's components failed the same way (MkCons) where
note: the JVM returns; they now take the target's component types. recorded.base is the reference frontend at B0.
recorded.jvm: Value 420102 []
recorded.base: Failure [] "MkCons: element type Bool[] does not match list element type Data[]"
---
import java.math.BigInteger;
import org.julclang.core.types.Tuple3;

public class Probe {

    public static byte[] m(BigInteger x, BigInteger y) {
        Tuple3<BigInteger, byte[], Boolean> t = new Tuple3<>(y, new byte[]{1, 2}, x.compareTo(y) < 0);
        return t.third() ? t.second() : new byte[]{};
    }
}
